  "externalFindings": {
    "identity": "2026–2027 standalone Leiden Astronomy BSc, BA-STK. The OER astronomy appendix pp. 42–48 separates the double degrees. Year 1 mainly Dutch, year 2 Dutch and English, year 3 English.",
    "year1": "60 EC of required introductory mathematics, computing, physics and astronomy. Experimental Physics I and Practical Astronomy contribute practical training alongside analysis, mechanics, electromagnetism and introductory astrophysics.",
    "year2": "60 EC required. Optics, statistical physics, quantum mechanics and more mathematics underpin astronomy modules on stars, galaxies and observing techniques. Practical Astronomy precedes the observing lab. The current observing module expects calculus, optics, Python and introductory astrophysics.",
    "year3": "30 EC approved free choice in the first semester, 6 EC Radiative Processes and 2 EC Research Skills & Scientific Integrity, and 22 EC research split into three assessed modules. Radiative Processes assumes prior classical electrodynamics and related physics.",
    "freeChoice": "OER appendix section 2.2 allows an approved minor, relevant electives or an individually approved package including study abroad. Level and non-overlap rules apply. The catalogue elective examples carry no universal requirement.",
    "progression": "OER appendix section 3.1 requires completing the first two years before the bachelor research project, with exceptions subject to authorization. The current research module describes a 20-week Leiden Observatory group project usually in pairs, subject to permission, with research, oral presentation and thesis credited separately."
  },
